.TH "CONDINAPT\-MINIOS" "7" "August 2026" "MiniOS CondinAPT Integration" ""
.SH NAME
condinapt\-minios \- CondinAPT integration in the MiniOS build system
.SH DESCRIPTION
This document describes the specific aspects of using
\f[B]condinapt\f[R](1) in the MiniOS build system.
.PP
For basic CondinAPT features, see \f[B]condinapt\f[R](1).
.SH INTEGRATION WITH MINIOS BUILD SYSTEM
.SS Usage in MiniOS Modules
CondinAPT is a standard tool for package installation in MiniOS modules.
It integrates into the build process through the standard module
interface.
.PP
In the module installation script (\f[B]install\f[R]):
.IP
.EX
#!/bin/bash
set \-e

# Load MiniOS library
\&. /minioslib || exit 1

# Install packages via CondinAPT
/usr/share/minios\-live/condinapt \[rs]
    \-l \[dq]$CWD/packages.list\[dq] \[rs]
    \-c /etc/minios\-live/build.conf \[rs]
    \-m /usr/share/minios\-live/condinapt.map
.EE
.SS MiniOS Module Structure
Each module in \f[B]/usr/share/minios\-live/scripts/\f[R] follows a
standardized structure:
.IP
.EX
XX\-module\-name/
├── packages.list                     # Package list with conditions
├── install                           # Installation script (uses CondinAPT)
├── rootcopy\-install/                 # (optional) Files to copy
└── rootcopy\-postinstall/             # (optional) Files after installation
.EE
.SH MINIOS CONFIGURATION
.SS Filter Mapping
Contents of \f[B]condinapt.map\f[R] in MiniOS:
.IP
.EX
d=DISTRIBUTION
da=DISTRIBUTION_ARCH
dp=DISTRIBUTION_PROFILE
is=INIT_SYSTEM
de=DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENT
pv=PACKAGE_VARIANT
ik=INSTALL_KERNEL
kf=KERNEL_FLAVOUR
kp=KERNEL_PROVIDER
kc=KERNEL_CAPABILITIES
kbd=KERNEL_BUILD_DKMS
ib=INITRAMFS_BUILDER
lo=LOCALE
ml=MULTILINGUAL
kl=KEEP_LOCALES
.EE
.SS Configuration Variables
Main variables from \f[B]build.conf\f[R]:
.TP
\f[B]DISTRIBUTION\f[R]
Target distribution (bookworm, trixie, jammy, noble)
.TP
\f[B]DISTRIBUTION_ARCH\f[R]
Architecture (amd64, i386, i386\-pae)
.TP
\f[B]DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENT\f[R]
Desktop environment (core, flux, xfce, lxqt)
.TP
\f[B]PACKAGE_VARIANT\f[R]
Package variant (minimum, standard, toolbox, ultra)
.TP
\f[B]INSTALL_KERNEL\f[R]
Install kernel package (true/false)
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_FLAVOUR\f[R]
Kernel flavour (none, rt, cloud)
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_PROVIDER\f[R]
Kernel package provider (distribution, minios)
.TP
\f[B]MINIOS_KERNEL_SERIES\f[R]
MiniOS kernel series (auto, 6.1, 6.12)
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_CAPABILITIES\f[R]
Capabilities detected from the selected kernel, such as aufs or ntfs3
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_PAYLOAD_MODE\f[R]
Kernel module payload mode (runtime, full)
.TP
\f[B]KERNEL_BUILD_DKMS\f[R]
Build DKMS modules (true/false)
.TP
\f[B]INITRAMFS_BUILDER\f[R]
Initramfs builder (livekit, dracut)
.TP
\f[B]LOCALE\f[R]
System locale (C, en_US, ru_RU, es_ES, pt_BR)
.TP
\f[B]MULTILINGUAL\f[R]
Multilingual support (true/false)
.TP
\f[B]KEEP_LOCALES\f[R]
Keep locales (true/false)
.SS Automatically Calculated Variables
From \f[B]minioslib\f[R]:
.TP
\f[B]DISTRIBUTION_PROFILE\f[R]
Distribution behavior profile (debian, ubuntu) \- automatically
determined based on DISTRIBUTION
.TP
\f[B]INIT_SYSTEM\f[R]
Init system profile (systemd, sysvinit) \- automatically determined
based on DISTRIBUTION
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Multimedia Module
\f[B]packages.list:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
# Basic multimedia codecs \- always
gstreamer1.0\-plugins\-base
gstreamer1.0\-plugins\-good

# Additional codecs \- not for minimal variant
gstreamer1.0\-plugins\-bad \-pv=minimum
gstreamer1.0\-plugins\-ugly \-pv=minimum
gstreamer1.0\-libav \-pv=minimum

# Professional tools \- only for toolbox and ultra
audacity +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra}
kdenlive +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra} +{de=xfce|de=lxqt}
\-\-\-
# Distribution\-specific packages from backports
ffmpeg \[at]bookworm\-backports +d=bookworm
.EE
.SS Driver Module
\f[B]packages.list:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
# Basic drivers
mesa\-utils
xserver\-xorg\-video\-all

# NVIDIA drivers \- only for non\-free distributions
nvidia\-driver +d=bookworm \-{pv=minimum&de=core}

# AMD drivers \- for modern distributions
firmware\-amd\-graphics +{d=trixie|d=noble}
mesa\-vulkan\-drivers +{d=trixie|d=noble}

# Old drivers \- for old systems
xserver\-xorg\-video\-radeon +d=bookworm
.EE
.SS Localization Module
\f[B]packages.list:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
# Basic locales \- always
locales

# Russian localization
language\-pack\-ru +lo=ru_RU
fonts\-liberation +lo=ru_RU
firefox\-esr\-l10n\-ru +lo=ru_RU +{de=xfce|de=lxqt}

# Multilingual support
task\-russian +ml=true +lo=ru_RU
hunspell\-ru +ml=true +lo=ru_RU

# Keeping locales
vlc\-l10n +kl=true +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra}

# Regional settings for different locales
language\-pack\-pt +lo=pt_BR
language\-pack\-de +lo=de_DE
language\-pack\-fr +lo=fr_FR
.EE
.SS Advanced Filter Usage
\f[B]packages.list:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
# DKMS modules with kernel and distribution conditions
ntfs3\-dkms \-kc=ntfs3
zfs\-dkms +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra} +da=amd64 +kbd=true \-kf=none

# Drivers for old systems
broadcom\-sta\-dkms \-d=jammy \-da=i386
aufs\-dkms +dp=debian +d=buster \-kc=aufs

# Exclusion when the selected kernel already provides the driver
realtek\-rtl8821cu\-dkms \-kc=rtw88_8821cu
firmware\-b43\-installer \-d=bionic

# Complex alternatives with filters
exfatprogs \-pv=minimum || exfat\-utils \-pv=minimum && exfat\-fuse \-pv=minimum

# Localization with exclusions and conditions
vlc\-l10n \-lo=en_US +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra}
language\-pack\-gnome\-ru\-base +lo=ru_RU +dp=ubuntu
language\-pack\-gnome\-ru\-base +ml=true +dp=ubuntu
language\-pack\-gnome\-ru\-base +kl=true +dp=ubuntu
.EE
.SS Optimization for MiniOS
Grouping by functionality:
.IP
.EX
#=== Core System ===
systemd +pv=standard +pv=toolbox +pv=ultra
dbus

#=== Desktop Environment ===
xfce4\-panel +de=xfce
lxqt\-panel +de=lxqt
fluxbox +de=flux

#=== Applications by Variant ===
firefox\-esr +{pv=standard|pv=toolbox|pv=ultra}
thunderbird +{pv=toolbox|pv=ultra}
libreoffice +pv=ultra
.EE
.SH INTEGRATION WITH BUILD PROCESS
.SS Module Environment Variables
Within the MiniOS module context, the following variables are available:
.TP
\f[B]$CWD\f[R]
Current module directory
.TP
\f[B]$LIVEKITNAME\f[R]
System name (usually \[lq]minios\[rq])
.TP
\f[B]$MODULE\f[R]
Current module name
.SS Using minioslib
Example installation script with conditional execution:
.IP
.EX
#!/bin/bash
set \-e

# Load MiniOS library
\&. /minioslib || exit 1

# Check module conditions
if [ \[dq]$PACKAGE_VARIANT\[dq] = \[dq]minimum\[dq] ] && [ \[dq]$DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENT\[dq] = \[dq]core\[dq] ]; then
    echo \[dq]Skipping module for minimal core build\[dq]
    exit 0
fi

# Install packages
/usr/share/minios\-live/condinapt \[rs]
    \-l \[dq]$CWD/packages.list\[dq] \[rs]
    \-c /etc/minios\-live/build.conf \[rs]
    \-m /usr/share/minios\-live/condinapt.map
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
\f[B]/etc/minios\-live/build.conf\f[R]
Main MiniOS build configuration file
.TP
\f[B]/usr/share/minios\-live/condinapt.map\f[R]
Filter mapping for MiniOS build system
.TP
\f[B]/usr/share/minios\-live/scripts/XX\-module\-name/packages.list\f[R]
Package list for each module
.TP
\f[B]/usr/share/minios\-live/scripts/XX\-module\-name/install\f[R]
Module installation script
